body:
I'm generally against APIs that call `Entity.update` inside of them -- this makes batching multiple updates impossible. We should instead have the consumer call `Entity.update`.

```ts
Entity.update(x, (x) => {
   Entity.setConvergenceKey(x, 'foo')
})
```

...but then do we even need a separate function? why not:

```ts
Entity.update(x, (x) => {
   Entity.getMeta(x).convergenceKey = 'foo'
})
```

